# Loaded automatically by `next build` (Next.js's built-in env file
# convention - .env.production is read whenever NODE_ENV=production, which
# `next build` sets internally). This is what actually fixes GA4 event
# tracking in the Docker/Cloud Run build: NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars get compiled
# directly into the client-side JS bundle at build time, not read from
# process.env at runtime like server code - so setting this only as a Cloud
# Run runtime env var (Variables & Secrets in the console) has no effect on
# the client bundle at all. Committed to git rather than kept secret because
# a GA4 Measurement ID isn't sensitive - it's already visible to anyone who
# views the page source of the deployed site.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-N11473XXZN
